{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-spawn-vessel-002-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/SpawnSafetyNetTests.cs", "line": 1485, "method": "ComputeRecordedTerminalOrbitMeanAnomalyAtUT_ShiftsToSpawnUT", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/VesselSpawner.cs:6049; return rec.TerminalOrbitMeanAnomalyAtEpoch instead of delegating -> red", "what_it_asserts": "the SUT result equals TimeJumpManager.ComputeEpochShiftedMeanAnomaly called inline with the same arguments", "why_weak": "the oracle is the SUT's own delegate, so any change inside ComputeEpochShiftedMeanAnomaly moves both sides together and the name's claim (that the anomaly is SHIFTED to the spawn UT) is never pinned", "proposed_action": "assert against a hand-computed value for the pinned SMA/mu/dt, or at minimum Assert.NotEqual(rec.TerminalOrbitMeanAnomalyAtEpoch, actual)", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
